      "level": 1,
      "ordinal": 7,
      "summary": "WAF - USA (130kt) On average since January 2000, VLCCs have earned $56,000 per day as compared to Suezmaxes which have earned $39,000 per day - a difference of $17,000 per day which is enough of a margin even for today's newbuilding prices. In the past 18 months, however, this differential has nearly doubled to over $30,000 per day in these two markets suggesting that the spread in earnings appears to be outweighing the spread in the asset prices.",
